    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "## Goal\nImplement native [Landlock](https://landlock.io/) sandboxing to restrict qTox filesystem access. Unlike AppArmor, Landlock is unprivileged and works regardless of installation method (Flatpak, AppImage, etc.).\n\n## Implementation Plan\n\n### 1. Hierarchical Sandboxing\nUse Landlock's thread-scoped enforcement for granular protection:\n\n*   **Global Baseline:** Applied in `AppManager` at startup. Inherited by all threads.\n    *   **Read-Only:** `/usr`, `/lib`, `/etc`, `/usr/share`.\n    *   **Read-Write:** qTox config and data directories (`~/.config/tox`, `~/.cache/qTox`).\n    *   **Denied:** All other paths (e.g., `~/.ssh`, `~/.bashrc`).\n\n*   **Thread-Specific Restrictions:** Major components drop additional privileges on thread entry:\n    *   **Toxcore:** Drops all FS access except the active `.tox` profile and network sockets.\n    *   **History:** Limits access strictly to the SQLite database file.\n    *   **AV:** Limits access to `/dev/video*` and `/dev/snd*`.\n\n### 2. Access Policy (ABI v3)\n\n| Access | Target |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **RW** | Profile & Settings (`Paths::getSettingsDirPath()`) |\n| **RW** | Configured Downloads Directory |\n| **RO** | System libs, Fonts, Themes (`/usr`, `/etc`, `~/.fonts`) |\n| **IO** | Media devices (`/dev/video*`, `/dev/snd*`, `/dev/dri/*`) |\n\n### 3. Implementation Notes\n*   **Initialization:** Use `syscall()` in `src/platform/linux/landlock.cpp` for kernel/glibc compatibility.\n*   **ABI Support:** Support ABI v1-v3, utilizing `TRUNCATE` and `REFER` where available.\n*   **Configuration:** \n    *   Enable via `--landlock` flag for testing.\n    *   Paths must be defined before calling `landlock_restrict_self`. Dynamic download path changes may require a restart.\n\n## Advantages\n- **Exploit Mitigation:** Isolates the filesystem from network-facing code.\n- **Portability:** Automatic protection without external tools or system configuration.\n- **Efficiency:** Minimal kernel-level overhead.\n",
